Subject: [PATCH 9/9] hw/misc/esp32_ledc, hw/misc/tbi_bridge, hw/xtensa/esp32:
 LEDC waveforms to the TBI host

Replace the upstream duty-percentage stub with the LEDC register semantics (TRM v5.8 ch. 28,
IDF ledc_ll): timers (clock source, 10.8 divider, resolution, reset, pause), channels (timer
binding, output enable, idle level, hpoint and duty latched at duty_start), DUTY_R, the counter
derived from virtual time. Publish each high-speed timer and channel state change to the bridge
as P and W frames (capability pwm); the host computes the waveform. Dither, fade, interrupts,
the low-speed group and wrapping hpoint/duty are reported unsupported. APB follows the SoC clock.
