+ *
+ * This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the
+ * GNU General Public License version 2 or (at your option) any later version.
+ *
+ * Clean-room from the ESP32 Technical Reference Manual v5.8, chapter 28 (LED_PWM) and the ESP-IDF
+ * register layout (soc/esp32/include/soc/ledc_reg.h, hal/esp32/include/hal/ledc_ll.h). The model
+ * produces no edges: each change of a high-speed timer or channel is published to the TBI bridge
+ * (capability "pwm") as a complete description, from which the host computes the waveform exactly:
+ *
+ *   timer   P <vns> <timer> run <clk_hz> <div> <res>   counter running: tick = div / 256 source
+ *                                                       clocks (10.8 fixed point), period 2^res ticks
+ *           P <vns> <timer> reset | paused              counter held
+ *           P <vns> <timer> unsupported <why>           a configuration this model cannot represent
+ *   channel W <vns> <sig> idle <level>                  output disabled: the idle level
+ *           W <vns> <sig> on <timer> <hpoint> <duty>    output high from counter = hpoint for duty
+ *                                                       ticks of every period (duty <= 2^res)
+ *           W <vns> <sig> unsupported <why>
+ *
+ * <sig> is the GPIO-matrix output signal (LEDC_HS_SIG_OUT0..7 = 71..78), as in the bridge's F
+ * frames, so the host joins waveforms to pads through the routing it already receives.
+ *
+ * Semantics (TRM ch. 28; IDF ledc.h): a channel's duty and hpoint take effect only with duty_start,
+ * and only at the next PWM cycle; a high-speed timer's new parameters take effect at its next
+ * overflow (glitch-free change-over); releasing a timer's reset restarts its counter at 0. The host
+ * applies those rules; this device reports the register state and the virtual time of each change.
+ *
+ * Refused, never approximated: duty dithering (DUTY[3:0] != 0: the TRM's "statistical" extra
+ * cycle has no documented generator), hardware fading (duty_scale != 0), LEDC interrupts, the
+ * low-speed group (separate para_up update rules and clock selection), an hpoint/duty pair that
+ * wraps past the counter's period, a divider below 1.0 and a resolution outside 1..20 bits.
+ * The source clocks are the modelled APB clock (property "apb-freq", kept current by the SoC) and
+ * REF_TICK, which ESP-IDF always configures to 1 MHz.
+ */
